  "body": "## What happens\n\nA tool with no number of its own posts as its 1-based position in the document's tool list (`crates/app/src/tool_numbers.rs`, #221), and that list is in name order. Adding a tool whose name sorts earlier renumbers every tool after it. Re-posting the same operations after adding a tool changes the T/H words of tools the operator has already loaded and touched off.\n\n## Evidence (upstream main abe24ff09)\n\nQA project tools, `posts_as` before: CM-1000-90 = 1, DR-0600 = 2, EM-0600-4FL = 3, EM-1000-4FL = 4, SPOT-0600-90 = 5, SPOT-CM-0600-90 = 6. After `add_tool {catalog: \"EM-0600-4FL\", name: \"AA-FIRST\"}`: AA-FIRST = 1, CM-1000-90 = 2, DR-0600 = 3, EM-0600-4FL = 4, EM-1000-4FL = 5, SPOT-0600-90 = 6, SPOT-CM-0600-90 = 7. `number` stays null on all of them. In the QA run, adding `SPOT-0600-90` moved `SPOT-CM-0600-90` from T5 to T6.\n\nA program posted before and after the add calls the same end mill T4 and then T5. On a PathPilot table set from the first program, `T5 M6 / G43 H5` loads the old T5 and its length offset: a wrong tool and a wrong Z. The program itself is consistent, so nothing in CamCraft can catch it.\n\n## Expected\n\nA tool's posted number is stable once the tool is in the document: e.g. `add_tool` gives the next free number (and says so), or unnumbered tools keep the number they first posted with, and a post with unnumbered tools says which numbers it assumed.\n\nP3 (not P1): the shift needs a controller table set from an earlier post; the setup sheet and program comments name each T. Raise it if the maintainer reads the re-post case as wrong output.\n\nFound by the QA swarm (SolidCraft v0.44.1 + CamCraft v0.23.0, part p01-flange). Re-checked on upstream main abe24ff09.\n\n**Done means:** adding, renaming or deleting a tool never changes another tool's posted T/H number; pinned by a test that posts, adds an earlier-sorting tool and posts again with the same T words.\n",
